{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main(){\n    int x, y, n;\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &x, &y, &n);\n    int g = __gcd(x, y);\n    x /= g;\n    y /= g;\n\n    const long double d = 1.0;\n    const long double eps = 1e-10;\n    const long double reference = d * x / y;\n\n    long long xx = 0;\n    long long ansX = 0, ansY = 1;\n\n    auto error = [&](long long num, long long den)->long double {\n        return abs(reference - d * num / den);\n    };\n\n    for(long long yy = 1; yy <= n; ++yy){\n        while(error(xx, yy) > error(xx + 10000, yy))\n            xx += 10000;\n        while(error(xx, yy) + eps > error(xx + 1, yy))\n            ++xx;\n        if(error(xx, yy) < error(ansX, ansY)){\n            ansX = xx;\n            ansY = yy;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld/%lld\\n\", max(0LL, ansX - (y == 2 && ansX != x)), ansY);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    x, y, n = map(int, data[:3])\n    g = math.gcd(x, y)\n    x //= g\n    y //= g\n\n    d = 1.0\n    eps = 1e-10\n    reference = d * x / y\n\n    xx = 0\n    ansX = 0\n    ansY = 1\n\n    def error(num, den):\n        return abs(reference - d * num / den)\n\n    for yy in range(1, n + 1):\n        while error(xx, yy) > error(xx + 10000, yy):\n            xx += 10000\n        while error(xx, yy) + eps > error(xx + 1, yy):\n            xx += 1\n        if error(xx, yy) < error(ansX, ansY):\n            ansX = xx\n            ansY = yy\n\n    # Adjust ansX as in original code\n    if y == 2 and ansX != x:\n        ansX -= 1\n    ansX = max(0, ansX)\n\n    print(f\"{ansX}/{ansY}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00033444532891735435, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0005569098866544664, -0.000169382052263245, -0.029750416055321693, -0.0024850459303706884, -0.00043072958942502737, 0.0, -0.00043394684325903654, -0.00026901919045485556, -0.015385630540549755, -0.011049510911107063, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.08280454576015472, 0.0, -8.737658936297521e-05, 0.0, -0.006715467199683189, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.008614758029580116, -0.00012337400403339416, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.876845170860179e-05, -0.023245912045240402, 0.0, -0.00012385078298393637, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -7.033323527139146e-06, -0.07898459583520889, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.125986263010418e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.002248499309644103, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.014187542721629143, -0.008614876307547092, -0.0007240534760057926, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.4543427823809907e-05, -3.099436753473128e-06, 0.0, -0.008615585044026375, -2.384185